1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,620
Your company's AI chatbot isn't dumb.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,859
It just never read your documents.

3
00:00:04,899 --> 00:00:06,300
Ask it your refund policy,

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:08,447
and it'll confidently make one up.

5
00:00:08,472 --> 00:00:09,780
And the fix isn't a bigger

6
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:10,459
model.

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,299
It's a trick called RAG.

8
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:13,540
Think of it like an open-book

9
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:14,340
exam.

10
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,673
Before the model answers,

11
00:00:15,727 --> 00:00:16,980
it searches your documents,

12
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:18,660
grabs the three paragraphs that match

13
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:19,753
the question best,

14
00:00:19,807 --> 00:00:21,300
and reads them first.

15
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,140
Behind the scenes,

16
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:24,020
every paragraph is turned into numbers

17
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,340
that capture its meaning,

18
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,327
and stored in a vector database.

19
00:00:27,353 --> 00:00:28,820
So it finds the right paragraph

20
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,780
even when you use different words.

21
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:32,020
That's why the answer comes back

22
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:33,420
with a source you can click.

23
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:34,847
And when the policy changes,

24
00:00:34,873 --> 00:00:36,420
you just update the document.

25
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,580
No retraining.

26
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,420
If you want to get into

27
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,420
AI engineering,

28
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:40,740
this is the first thing to

29
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:41,300
learn.

30
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:41,833
Follow,

31
00:00:41,887 --> 00:00:43,940
and next I'll explain AI agents.

